RuyaOS patch for xwayland-satellite (RUY-434, ADR-034). Written against 0.8.3.

What: when an output has no name (wl_output before version 4 has no name
event), call it "WL-<n>", n being its wl_registry global name, instead of
unwrapping a name that never arrives.

Why: QtWaylandCompositor offers wl_output version 2 (hard-coded in qtwayland).
Unpatched, the satellite panics with MissingComponent(OutputName) as soon as
an X window takes keyboard focus or enters an output (RUY-1, Dell). The name
is only used to pick the X primary output; with no name event Xwayland names
its RandR output itself, so the satellite logs "Couldn't find output WL-<n>,
primary output will be wrong" and keeps the primary output it has, which is
the only output on a console.

Upstream state: not offered upstream (owner decision). Drop this patch once
qtwayland offers wl_output >= 4 or upstream stops unwrapping the name.

--- a/src/server/event.rs
+++ b/src/server/event.rs
@@ -1005,7 +1005,14 @@
 pub(super) struct OnOutput(pub Entity);
 struct OutputName(String);
 fn get_output_name(output: Option<&OnOutput>, world: &World) -> Option<String> {
-    output.map(|o| world.get::<&OutputName>(o.0).unwrap().0.clone())
+    output.map(|o| match world.get::<&OutputName>(o.0) {
+        Ok(name) => name.0.clone(),
+        // wl_output before version 4 has no name event: name the output after its global.
+        Err(_) => format!(
+            "WL-{}",
+            world.get::<&GlobalName>(o.0).map(|g| g.0).unwrap_or(0)
+        ),
+    })
 }

 #[derive(Copy, Clone, PartialEq, Debug)]
